ner.<br /> <br /> But they should be interesting</div> </div> </div> </div>How early are we talking? Any idea what your target era is, or are you thinking any time before DA?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:15:31-08:00","id":368715,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking either prehistoric/Stone Age ( early settlement) or bronze Age Mesopotamia. I'm looking at an idealist guiding early Man in toolmaking/improving upon tools","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 01-13-2015, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T18:34:32-08:00","id":369268,"title":"","content":"OK I'll admit, I'm so wound up...its giving me writer's block, I stare blankly at the screen, I have the information I'm just not sure how to write it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T05:37:45-08:00","id":369698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=369268#post369268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK I'll admit, I'm so wound up...its giving me writer's block, I stare blankly at the screen, I have the information I'm just not sure how to write it down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I trick I use in those case, is to put doen my idea on paper randomly. Words, bits of sentences, arrows and drawing. Once the ideas are down I can play with it or let it sit for a bit and return later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T06:22:20-08:00","id":383006,"title":"","content":"One of my alternate tribes is an alternate take on the Glass Walkers, giving them a specifically classical Roman origin and Roman motifs. Legend says that the Glass Walkers were founded by the She-Wolf who fed Romulus and Remus. The Julio-Claudian dynasty were distant Glass Walker kinfolk (though Caligula was corrupted by the Wyrm) and the later Emperors Diocletian and Julian the Apostate were very notable and heroic Glass Walkers, protecting both the Garou of the Roman Empire and the humans and wolves of Rome as best they could.<br /> <br /> Caligula, Nero, Commodus, Constantine and Theodosius were all agents of the Wyrm. It is heavily rumored that Constantine may have been a Black Spiral Dancer sent to corrupt Rome from within.<br /> <br /> The Wise Guys camp were originally a Roman camp called the Patricians, and they maintained the name until the 20th Century. As the Wise Guys are losing influence, there is many talks of going into legitimate businesses and returning to their roots as the Patricians, noblemen and merchants of old.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I actually like when historical figures are supernatural entities in the Classic World of Darkness. And I do love Rome)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T09:13:00-08:00","id":383212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=383006#post383006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of my alternate tribes is an alternate take on the Glass Walkers, giving them a specifically classical Roman origin and Roman motifs. Legend says that the Glass Walkers were founded by the She-Wolf who fed Romulus and Remus. The Julio-Claudian dynasty were distant Glass Walker kinfolk (though Caligula was corrupted by the Wyrm) and the later Emperors Diocletian and Julian the Apostate were very notable and heroic Glass Walkers, protecting both the Garou of the Roman Empire and the humans and wolves of Rome as best they could.<br /> <br /> Caligula, Nero, Commodus, Constantine and Theodosius were all agents of the Wyrm. It is heavily rumored that Constantine may have been a Black Spiral Dancer sent to corrupt Rome from within.<br /> <br /> The Wise Guys camp were originally a Roman camp called the Patricians, and they maintained the name until the 20th Century. As the Wise Guys are losing influence, there is many talks of going into legitimate businesses and returning to their roots as the Patricians, noblemen and merchants of old.<br /> <br /> (Yes, I actually like when historical figures are supernatural entities in the Classic World of Darkness. And I do love Rome)</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually have a write up for the She-Wolf, Asena, as a totem. She is one of the few totems I allow Ronin characters to take during creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T17:57:10-08:00","id":399629,"title":"","content":"So, Celts concept gave me an idea. I am working on a North American group. Each individual tribe will be based loosely on the tribes from Forsaken. I am using the Translation guide as template but I am making a few changes to better suit my concepts and a few to just make things flow a little better. Example, the Blood Talons with be the Blood Song and they will follow Wolverine. The name change is simply because having the Red Talons and the Blood Talons seemed a little much and I think wolverine fits the tribe as I have read in a better way. As always, when i have something of value I will post it and I always like to hear feedback lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T18:53:12-08:00","id":399719,"title":"","content":"Should I not bother posting mine then? I want to get to it but the writer's block's been pretty bad. I've been nervous as to how to go about writing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T18:56:13-08:00","id":399720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=399719#post399719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I not bother posting mine then? I want to get to it but the writer's block's been pretty bad. I've been nervous as to how to go about writing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would post it if you find the words. People may like your version more then mine. I may like yours more then mine, I can be fickle like that lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T04:02:24-08:00","id":400165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=399719#post399719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should I not bother posting mine then? I want to get to it but the writer's block's been pretty bad. I've been nervous as to how to go about writing it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And people could also give you ideas to help alleviate said writer block<br /> <br /> (and I need to complete mine, crazy feww weeks).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T08:03:26-08:00","id":400321,"title":"","content":"For me, I have a lot of books on the East both history books and legends. The idea of the Council of the Emerald Lady is fascinating, but I feel some of the members needed to change to joining to make a stronger idea of an Eastern Run Shifter Game. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HAKKEN</b><br /> <br /> I have found in my opinion the Hakken, the Japanese Samurai Werewolves, that are members of the Shadow Lords makes to me no sense. I understand that White Wolf did not have an idea of the East much at that time nor how global their Shapeshifting game would be. Heck when the Hakken were made no one had thought of the Council of the Emerald Lady. After all the great Japanese Stories if you read them involve a lot of Samurai (Hakken) fighting Spider Kami (Kumo). They are also known for their battles with the Kui-Jin as well. <br /> <br /> So in my game, the Hakken are a Tribe of Japanese Werewolves, pretty much how they are already written but with some changes, with no ties to the Shadow Lords they are a Tribe of their own and always have been believing that their origins come from the Sun God and Moon Goddess (keep terms simple here). They are members of the Council of the Emerald Lady and are known for their Strict Code of Honor, which they have a mystical tie to this makes sense in their new Write Up in <b>W20 pages 506-507</b>.<br /> <br /> Their Tribal Weakness is if they break their form of Garou Bushido they can't access their Gifts until they make amends usually it is done in the form of Sappaku or they can go on an epic quest to regain their Honor, which is a suicide mission. I admit I took the old Bushi Vampire Clan Weakness and worked on it for a Garou instead. Since the Bushi no longer exist since Kindred of the East, but instead one of the Dharmas in Vancouver Dark Alliance errata and in Shadow War, Yokoshi is listed as a Kui-Jin, the game designers said they had not thought of the Kui-Jin when they made Vancouver. I thought taking the Bushi weakness it would make a good Tribal Weakness for the Hakken than a Kindred. <br /> <br /> The Hakken in the Modern Day battle over Tradition and the ever expanding world around them between Tradition and Modernization and the whole East meets West viewpoint that Japanese even today deal with. The expansion of Women's roles especially Ahroun in the Hakken is still something the Tribe is dealing with. Their old isolationist views are challenged in the modern age. Their dwindling lupus population is a major concern. The loss of their Caerns in Hiroshima and Nagasaki due to the Atom Bombs being dropped can never be forgiven by many as the Wyrm snatched up what was left and twisted the rest. The Hakken blame the West for this corruption and infestation of the Wyrm in two of their cities. <br /> <br /> They view the Stargazers as too passive when in times they should have fought. <br /> <br /> Most of my notes are hand written and not transferred it over to a file yet. I changed some of their history using some of my books on Japanese Legends and History. <br /> <br /> Still struggling with the idea of finding a good Tribal Totem that reflects the Hakken as a Tribe. I need to go though my Hengoyaki and Japanese Legends to find a good mystical Patron for the Tribe. <br /> <br /> <b>STARGAZERS</b><br /> <br /> To me in Revised it made a lot of sense that the Stargazers are in the Council of the Emerald Lady not the Garou Nation as a whole. I have them in both as a Tribe but their real power are back East. Stargazers' viewpoint in many ways matches the beliefs. I felt that way when Henoyaki came out and was surprised the Stargazers were not members. I made this change. Disagree or agree I think it makes sense. In my W20 game they are members of both trying to mediate between the Garou Nation and the Council of the Emerald Lady. <br /> <br /> <b>BOLI ZOUSIZHE</b><br /> <br /> I have them as members of the Council of the Emerald Lady, no one trusts them because of their affiliation to Cockroach (insect totems are the sign of the Wyrm to Eastern Shifters) but like their former Warders of Man kin, they have embraced their take on technology at an earlier stage than even the Warders now Glass Walkers. The stories of great Chinese and Asian technology in ancient times to today can be associated many of them to the Bolo Zousizhe. The Kitsune find them fascinating and the Foxes want to know how things work. It was the Kitsune who wanted them as members and they found their way in. Others think the Kitsune's fascination is going to ruin them all. Others think the Kitsune might be keeping them close for a watchful eye. Who knows what is going on in a Fox's mind. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T10:26:54-08:00","id":400490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=400321#post400321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>HAKKEN</b><br /> Still struggling with the idea of finding a good Tribal Totem that reflects the Hakken as a Tribe. I need to go though my Hengoyaki and Japanese Legends to find a good mystical Patron for the Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>You actually aren't far off with what you believe about the Hakken. There is a small side note in the Hengeyokai book about the fact that they used to have a different patron spirit, a different asain themed storm spirit, and were pretty much their own unique tribe. Their totem, Susanowo - The Lord of Storms, simply vanished one day and hasn't been heard from since. Grand Father Thunder (Naru-Kami) swooped in and assimilated them into the Shadowlord (with a health noting that it was probably GFT that made their totem disappear). I think having them find their original totem being held hostage by GFT would make for an interesting story line and establish them again as their own unique tribe. <br /> <br /> I also agree with you about the Stargazers. When they made the Hengeyokai a thing it really made the Stargazers being part of the Nation very strange. Their ideals flow better with the Emerald Court and based on location it made more sense to ally with them as well.<br /> <br /> I could see the Boli Zousizhe following Fox as their tribal totem, it was the recommended totem after all for the Iron Masters in the Translation guide. Could make them another unique tribe in the east and strengthen the link with the Kitsune while removing a little bit of the pariah feel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-10T12:30:40-08:00","id":400687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=400490#post400490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You actually aren't far off with what you believe about the Hakken. There is a small side note in the Hengeyokai book about the fact that they used to have a different patron spirit, a different asain themed storm spirit, and were pretty much their own unique tribe. Their totem, Susanowo - The Lord of Storms, simply vanished one day and hasn't been heard from since. Grand Father Thunder (Naru-Kami) swooped in and assimilated them into the Shadowlord (with a health noting that it was probably GFT that made their totem disappear). I think having them find their original totem being held hostage by GFT would make for an interesting story line and establish them again as their own unique tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am aware of Susanowo-The Lord of Storms, but so sure he was the right Totem to begin with. And in my game the Totem of the Hakken is already there, but I could have done a story of finding it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=400490#post400490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also agree with you about the Stargazers. When they made the Hengeyokai a thing it really made the Stargazers being part of the Nation very strange. Their ideals flow better with the Emerald Court and based on location it made more sense to ally with them as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think most people do. TheTribe leaving the Garou Nation made sense in Revised. It was one of the best ideas they had in it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=400490#post400490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see the Boli Zousizhe following Fox as their tribal totem, it was the recommended totem after all for the Iron Masters in the Translation guide. Could make them another unique tribe in the east and strengthen the link with the Kitsune while removing a little bit of the pariah feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Fox Totem has nothing to do with them. The Kitsune just find them interesting... or watching them... or both. They still have Cockroach right now, but I am thinking it could work better for something else like <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T10:07:58-07:00","id":458131,"title":"","content":"Hello everyone.<br /> I hadn't work on re-vamped Tribes, but in my chronicles, a Fire Elemental and Pain Spirit fused creating the Spirit know as the Fire Blood; this new Spirit start to act as patron for the characters pack, growing rapidly as they devote his success to it (spending experience to make it stronger); then many other cubs take it as a Pack totem, an it start to subdue some gafflings to its service, incrementing its sphere of power; when many members of the Sept acknowledg it like a strong Jaggling, it makes it's next move in it's agenda. Using the force of its servants, his familiarity with the internal sept guard, and when many pack were busy with Wyrm servants; the Fire Blood beat the Sept Totem and drained the Caern of its Gnosis (it used to be a Level 2 Caern).<br /> When the characters discover what it have done, Fire Blood express his ambition to become an Incarna, and the spiritual father of a new Garou tribe.<br /> <br /> Despite the fact that it had drained a Caern, many Cliaths, Cubs and Ronin began to follow it, and start to call themselves the Fire Blooded. Ultimately the characters defeat the Fire Blood and sent it to Slumber and bind it to an iron sword that was throwed into a chasm of a underground cave by the Ragabash of the pack. Now the Fire Blooded act more as a intertribal Camp compose by Ronin, some Shadow Lords, a pair of Fenrir and two Red Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5485-malakai","name":"Malakai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5485_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T01:56:56-07:00","id":458754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nene Richards</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=400321#post400321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, I have a lot of books on the East both history books and legends. The idea of the Council of the Emerald Lady is fascinating, but I feel some of the members needed to change to joining to make a stronger idea of an Eastern Run Shifter Game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>HAKKEN</b><br /> <br /> I have found in my opinion the Hakken, the Japanese Samurai Werewolves, that are members of the Shadow Lords makes to me no sense. I understand that White Wolf did not have an idea of the East much at that time nor how global their Shapeshifting game would be. Heck when the Hakken were made no one had thought of the Council of the Emerald Lady. After all the great Japanese Stories if you read them involve a lot of Samurai (Hakken) fighting Spider Kami (Kumo). They are also known for their battles with the Kui-Jin as well.<br /> <br /> So in my game, the Hakken are a Tribe of Japanese Werewolves, pretty much how they are already written but with some changes, with no ties to the Shadow Lords they are a Tribe of their own and always have been believing that their origins come from the Sun God and Moon Goddess (keep terms simple here). They are members of the Council of the Emerald Lady and are known for their Strict Code of Honor, which they have a mystical tie to this makes sense in their new Write Up in <b>W20 pages 506-507</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Scotland can have a seperate tribe from Celts and Norse/Germanic Damn well Japan can!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their Tribal Weakness is if they break their form of Garou Bushido they can't access their Gifts until they make amends usually it is done in the form of Sappaku or they can go on an epic quest to regain their Honor, which is a suicide mission. I admit I took the old Bushi Vampire Clan Weakness and worked on it for a Garou instead. Since the Bushi no longer exist since Kindred of the East, but instead one of the Dharmas in Vancouver Dark Alliance errata and in Shadow War, Yokoshi is listed as a Kui-Jin, the game designers said they had not thought of the Kui-Jin when they made Vancouver. I thought taking the Bushi weakness it would make a good Tribal Weakness for the Hakken than a Kindred. </div> </div> </div>Honestly I thought the Bushi flaw was a mistake. It a very 1 dimensional view of a very complex concept and one that isn't completely a timeless aspect of Japan. Perhaps making them more prone to frenzy but with most holding to Codes of honor to overcome this sort of thing?(Since it helps with Willpower)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hakken in the Modern Day battle over Tradition and the ever expanding world around them between Tradition and Modernization and the whole East meets West viewpoint that Japanese even today deal with. The expansion of Women's roles especially Ahroun in the Hakken is still something the Tribe is dealing with. Their old isolationist views are challenged in the modern age. Their dwindling lupus population is a major concern. The loss of their Caerns in Hiroshima and Nagasaki due to the Atom Bombs being dropped can never be forgiven by many as the Wyrm snatched up what was left and twisted the rest. The Hakken blame the West for this corruption and infestation of the Wyrm in two of their cities. </div> </div> </div>Well Lupus only exist in the World of Darkness because they are keeping afew wolves secret(Since IRL Native wolves are extinct in Japan.)<br /> <br /> I'd imagine The Hakken may also have signfiicant issues with dealing with the Japanese Atrocities during ww2, both the wyrm effects left over and anger that sets them apart from other Emerald courts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Still struggling with the idea of finding a good Tribal Totem that reflects the Hakken as a Tribe. I need to go though my Hengoyaki and Japanese Legends to find a good mystical Patron for the Tribe.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Bishamon, Seta kamuy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T03:23:47-07:00","id":458780,"title":"","content":"Interestingy I don't see female roles as much of a problem for Hakken. Garou are a meritocracy and all of them need to fight. One might guess the female Hakken were the inspiration for people like Tomoe Gozen. On the other hand I see the Hakken as being complicit in a lot of the Japanese WW2 stuff. Just like the Get culture, history and nationalism colored their actions and they may have done worse then their moral compass and duties to Gaia would have had them do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T10:14:46-07:00","id":471357,"title":"","content":"Alright I have a new concept for the Domini Canis I am tinkering with and I am not quite sure if its the right direction or not. I am thinking that their origin should start sometime during the War of Rage. Leaning towards a more Militant Faction of Children of Gaia that felt they weren't doing enough ultimately ending in them distancing themselves from the Garou Nation entirely. They become judge and jury of the other tribes holding them accountable for their actions, including any violation of the Litany, while seeking to honor those their kind has lost or destroyed.<br /> <br /> Their tribal religion preaches about The Creator, and the spirit that guides them is called different things; The Voice, The Messenger, or most often The Witness. Throughout history the spirit has appeared as notable seers to modern day sign holders on soap boxes preaching the end. They follow the Witness as their Tribal Totem but never follow him directly. Instead they are broken into Orders who follow the totem spirit of fallen Tribes/Fera. So there is the Order of the Golden Mane, Order of the Brazen Hoof, and Order of the Ivory Tusk; lead by Lion, Bull (In the form of Aurouch), and Boar. This leads to their Optional Tribal Flaw of Dual Loyalty; All tribesmen have to follow the ban of the Tribal Totem and the Totem of their Order.<br /> <br /> Implications of using this tribe in a game include Children of Gaia losing the Imminent Strike and Seekers of the Lost Tribes camps. <br /> <br /> Story lines include searching out and creating new orders around Bat, Turtle, &amp; Rainbow Serpent. Also, having distanced themselves from the Garou Nation they have managed to salvage relations with the other Fera though tenuous with some, so Canis mediators often interject themselves in any Garou / Fera conflict they can to strengthen these relations.<br /> <br /> Gifts: There is a list of tribal gifts that all members may pull from, and a few gifts unique to each Order. Order Gifts are lost if the Garou decides to to change Order. <br /> <br /> Ana, since they are your original concept, if you have any ideas or critiques I would be very interested in your feedback. Feed back from anyone is, as always, welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:11:05-07:00","id":504808,"title":"","content":"I know, I have been crazy busy and I haven't really posted anything new... BUT I was inspired by another post on the forum so I give you the Dao Mau, a Children of Gaia concept camp for the Hengeyokai. Unlike their western counterparts they have been accepted as emissaries and mediators. Still a work in progress<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8GVz-RVG_GBdDVBbExhWE9lS3M/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8G...ew?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry, just realized the sharing settings weren't right, should be able to view this now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","user":"Derzhuzad","date":". 05-06-2015, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:08:03-07:00","id":506351,"title":"","content":"It feels like its missing something. Why Vietnam vs any other random group? Maybe give some of the general Hengeyokai gifts as options for this group?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:32:07-07:00","id":506361,"title":"","content":"- Boli Zousizhe misspelled as Boli Zouhisze<br /> - Wisdom of the Ancient Ways is primarily a Philodox Gift.<br /> - Check spelling of Galliard in last Gift's system reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T04:24:03-07:00","id":506601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=506351#post506351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels like its missing something. Why Vietnam vs any other random group? Maybe give some of the general Hengeyokai gifts as options for this group?</div> </div> </div> </div>I settled on Vietnam because the internal strife in the country seemed like the kind of place that would attract Children of Gaia, and I wanted to associate this camp with local religion.<br /> <br /> As members of the Hengeyokai they have access to shared gifts just like the Hakken do. The gifts listed are gifts that are unique just to them, I should probably mention that in the beginning gifts section. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=506361#post506361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Boli Zousizhe misspelled as Boli Zouhisze<br /> - Wisdom of the Ancient Ways is primarily a Philodox Gift.<br /> - Check spelling of Galliard in last Gift's system reference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected. Thank You. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T05:03:00-07:00","id":506618,"title":"","content":"Vietnam doesn't seem to have a particularly violent history in comparison to anywhere else. It has issues in more recent times but that starts to get back to the &quot;We define CoG entirely by the 60s&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T05:22:35-07:00","id":506630,"title":"","content":"I wasn't looking for a place that was more violent then anywhere else. The area has had its share of a few feudal wars and dynasty change over but otherwise it is very stable. Their goal was only to get to a place where they could establish themselves in close proximity to the Beast Courts so that they could open dialog. This doesn't mean the don't exist in the rest of Asia, just that is the first place they established a foothold. That could simply be that they found a powerful site to open a Caern or Unicorn directed them to that place so as not to upset the already existing garou and fera of the region for their mission. <br /> <br /> I hadn't even considered the Vietnam war to be honest until you just now bring it up. If anything it would have probably caused internal struggles between them and the parent tribe, or at least those who sided with the humans that wanted to stay out of the conflict.<br /> <br /> As always I am open to suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T06:49:07-07:00","id":506713,"title":"","content":"The Vietnam war goes back to French colonialism and even further resistance to the Japanese while seized the Colony. And given Vietnam is attempting to build eco-tourism a Sept or two of CoG makes a fair amount of sense. The only major issue I have with Vietnam is the Nagah have according to their breed book colonised the area and consider the area second only to India as a homeland.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T07:45:47-07:00","id":506753,"title":"","content":"I don't have my books handy so correct me if I am not remembering it correctly, the Nagah are openly part of the Hengeyokai which means that once they were integrated in they would keep the Nagah's secret like all the others do. Before that, the Nagah would not kill them simply for being there. They would watch them closely and keep a healthy distance until they felt threatened. In my mind they wouldn't want to cause a conflict which could alert the rest of the Garou to their continued existence if it could be avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T14:36:21-07:00","id":507227,"title":"","content":"It's a bit iffy with Hengeyokai. They know about the Nagah, but they seem to keep very covert even there. It's even worse when you consider that they meet up with Stargazers, Boli Zouhisze, Indian Garou and shapeshifters unassociated with the Emerald Courts. They probably have to work quit hard at data compartmentalisation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T16:59:31-07:00","id":507394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=506713#post506713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vietnam war goes back to French colonialism and even further resistance to the Japanese while seized the Colony. And given Vietnam is attempting to build eco-tourism a Sept or two of CoG makes a fair amount of sense. The only major issue I have with Vietnam is the Nagah have according to their breed book colonised the area and consider the area second only to India as a homeland.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But there's lots of Colonialist issues through out the East. When are you imagining this group took root?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T04:21:24-07:00","id":507940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=353934#post353934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><i>Domini Canis</i></b></div> </div> </div> </div>I am a bit confused by this.<br /> <br /> In Latin it should mean &quot;<i><b>Lords of the Dog</b></i>&quot; or &quot;<i><b>...of the Dog Lord</b></i>&quot;<br /> <br /> I suspect that neither of them was the intended meaning...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T04:45:41-07:00","id":507943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LucaCherstich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=507940#post507940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a bit confused by this.<br /> In Latin it should mean &quot;<i><b>Lords of the Dog</b></i>&quot; or &quot;<i><b>...of the Dog Lord</b></i>&quot;<br /> I suspect that neither of them was the intended meaning...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it translates to Dog/Hound of the Lord, it is some reference to St. Dominic. Technically it should be Domini Canes since that is the plural syntax, that doesn't roll of the tongue as nicely. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=507394#post507394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's lots of Colonialist issues through out the East. When are you imagining this group took root?</div> </div> </div> </div>They would have taken root within the first few hundred years from when the Beast Courts started to form, this would have put them in a time frame where the Nagah were on the retreat and before the Stargazers ever joined the Nation. If someone choose to integrate them into their game I would put in the storyline options that their presence would have meant the Stargazers never joined the Nation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T10:21:35-07:00","id":508183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=507943#post507943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it translates to Dog/Hound of the Lord, it is some reference to St. Dominic. Technically it should be Domini Canes since that is the plural syntax, that doesn't roll of the tongue as nicely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the St. Dominic reference.<br /> I did not know about it!<br /> <br /> And regarding the language form: Ouch!<br /> I did not notice that most English-speakers would pronounce &quot;e&quot; with &quot;i&quot; (even if wrong in a Latin pronunciation)....<br /> It's just that, since I'm native Italian speaker, I tend to read things exactly as they are written...and so the whole thing sounded even odder !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5960,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","user":"LucaCherstich","date":". 05-08-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5960-lucacherstich","name":"LucaCherstich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T22:46:14-07:00","id":508770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=507943#post507943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would have taken root within the first few hundred years from when the Beast Courts started to form, this would have put them in a time frame where the Nagah were on the retreat and before the Stargazers ever joined the Nation. If someone choose to integrate them into their game I would put in the storyline options that their presence would have meant the Stargazers never joined the Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I am honestly not seeing the connection to Vietnam","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T11:33:40-07:00","id":509128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=508770#post508770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then I am honestly not seeing the connection to Vietnam</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess I am not understanding why you are caught up on the place they decided to stop being Vietnam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T18:56:16-07:00","id":509379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=509128#post509128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess I am not understanding why you are caught up on the place they decided to stop being Vietnam.</div> </div> </div> </div>'<br /> <br /> Why stop in a particular place? they have a bunch of powers based Vietnamese traditions but they don't feel particularly such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T19:23:53-07:00","id":509431,"title":"","content":"Why they stopped:<br /> The tribe or camp harried by the upheavals in France begin to spread out to French Colonies. They arrive in French Indo-China early in the history of the Colony. Within 2 generations they have become natives and slowly the Eurocentric group becomes native by the Second World War with very rare exceptions they are natives of Vietnam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T05:44:10-07:00","id":509812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=509431#post509431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why they stopped:<br /> The tribe or camp harried by the upheavals in France begin to spread out to French Colonies. They arrive in French Indo-China early in the history of the Colony. Within 2 generations they have become natives and slowly the Eurocentric group becomes native by the Second World War with very rare exceptions they are natives of Vietnam.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's very different than them being there since prehistoric times and makes abit more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-10T08:45:26-07:00","id":509871,"title":"","content":"Prehistoric Explanation, sometime in 7,000BCE the Vietnamese started to generate agriculture and pottery almost identical to that of Mesopotamia. This is one possible scenario that explains outsiders in Vietnam.<br /> <br /> Roman Explanation, 336 BCE - 323BCE, Alexander the Great marched and conquered from Europe to India, in his wake he left diplomats and soldiers in each area he conquered. If the CoG camp followed in their wake and decided to keep going after his death it would be easy to understand how they passed through Indian cultures until they finally came to the ocean on the east side of Vietnam and decided to stop.<br /> <br /> Silk Road Explanation, in the 1st Century BCE Romans began to create trade routes beyond the territory left by Alexander the Great, one of the stops for travelrs along the Silk Road was in Vietnam on the way to China.<br /> <br /> I will add these and Incbill's suggestion, if he is alright with it, to the Storyteller Options section.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T00:15:30-07:00","id":510486,"title":"","content":"No problems use whatever works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T04:31:25-07:00","id":510541,"title":"","content":"The more I think about them the more I like the idea of them following behead the Roman Expansion acting as diplomats and peacekeepers. Leads into them being the in the east for 300+ years before anyone traveling the silk roads would have seen them again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T12:12:38-07:00","id":518361,"title":"","content":"Ok, for the Dao Mau, I reworked the history a little to implement some of the things we came up with, still left it a little open ended. Started playing with the Dusk Walker's gift list. Thinking more gifts dealing with or from the shadowlands. These will replace gifts on the White Howler list that are from Lion or have to do with manipulating earth. The rationale is that they will be tied more strongly to the shadowlands then to Gaia. Toying with Carrion Bird as their totem, but that isn't definite yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-18T18:27:46-07:00","id":518630,"title":"","content":"Not so much an alternate tribe as a sub-group, but something I've been thinking about for a while due to the utter waste of lore I sometimes see in the Fenrir:<br /> <br /> <b>\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar</b> (northern Germanic), <b>Wargs</b> (western Germanic), Outlaws/Rebels/Vargr (to the Get of Fenris)<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Odin could make his enemies in battle blind, or deaf, or terror-struck, and their weapons so blunt that they could no more but than a willow wand; on the other hand, <b>his men rushed forwards without armor, were as mad as dogs or wolves, bit their shields, and were strong as bears or wild bulls, and killed people at a blow, but neither fire nor iron told upon themselves</b>.</i> - Heimskringla<br /> <br /> The Fenrir are some of the deadliest creatures to walk the earth, and they count as one of their greatest enemies Woden, a shamanic god-king they say walks with the Wyrm. They howl paeans to Luna, she of the changing face, a goddess incarnate in the sky. Somehow, these mighty beasts were unable to stop their Kinfolk from honoring Wyrm-folk as their gods.<br /> <br /> This is because the Fenrir lie. They are weak.<br /> <br /> Not in battle, no. Not in lore or song or history. But still, they are weak. They are outsiders amongst those they call Kin, they are the true vargr.<br /> <br /> When the ancestors of the Germanic peoples left central Asia for Europe, they took with them veneration of their ancestral gods, those the Fenrir call evil. For all their vaunted strength, the Fenrir could do little but call their gods monsters; they could never convert the folk to their ways, nor force the folk to their blasphemous subversions. Woden was a god, not a Wyrmthrall; the moon was Mani's face, not some Latinate goddess...all they agreed upon was that the earth was their Mother, and wolves were, indeed, holy. &quot;Mere humans&quot; defied them, for thousands of years, and always among them were the faithful, the true, Woden's wolves.<br /> <br /> Is it the way of a strong warrior to hide in the shadows like a Leech, proclaiming their dubious dominance? Is it holy to spit on the body of your people to follow some alien creed of moon-goddesses and evil ancestors?<br /> <br /> The \u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar, the Wargs, say no.<br /> <br /> They say it is the Fenrir who are weak. They say it is the Fenrir who are unholy. It is the Fenrir who spit upon the old ways. The Fenrir call them outlaws and rebels, but they know themselves as the true people of the north, holding fast to gods that were old when the Fenrir were still cubs. The Fenrir claim dominion among werewolves over the Germanic peoples (those who aren't Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia, or Glass Walkers, or Shadow Lords, or Silver Fangs), but they are little more than dogs, skulking in the darkness outside the people they claim, propagating a foreign creed because they were not strong enough to be true to their heritage.<br /> <br /> The Outlaws remain true to this day. A rebel camp within the Get of Fenris, a conspiracy of fanatic heathens, they are the werewolves who still feel the truth of their ancestral culture, rather than denigrating it, hiding from it and calling it &quot;weak.&quot; They organise in their own packs, when possible, and hold moots far from the eyes of the psychopaths who proudly proclaim their descent from a monster destined to help destroy a world.<br /> <br /> Ironically, their greatest allies in the World of Darkness are rarely other werewolves; among their kin they count all others who follow the ancestral ways, whether human or wizard or even draugr. The Garou (a name which, somewhat ironically to them, comes from the Frankish word for &quot;werewolf&quot;), are rarely willing to openly defy the Fenrir by succoring Wargs, but in multitribal septs without the presence of the Get, they do well. Unfortunately, most septs close to their Kinfolk contain Fenrir, so they range far and wide in the modern day, not unlike their human relations.<br /> <br /> Common totems of \u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar packs include Bear, Bull, Grandfather Thunder and Stag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/173-morimaruvik","name":"Morimaruvik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar173_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:11:47-08:00","id":753933,"title":"","content":"Sharing these two gifts because I wrote them for my write up on the Dusk Walkers but have gone a new way with them. Maybe someone here might have a use for them as gifts players have never seen for some new bad guy or maybe Silent Striders who have spent to much time in the dark umbra.<br /> <br /> Death\u2019s Caress (Rank 1)<br /> A fact that Dusk Walkers are intimately aware of is that death eventually comes for everyone. Most of the living (and many Undead) are unaware of how close they are to death every moment of they continue to walk Gaia. With this gift the Dusk Walker may instill the feeling of Death, true weakness and despair, in any creature they come into contact with.<br /> System: The Walker must touch the target\u2019s skin. The player rolls Rage (difficulty 6 for the living, 5 for the Undead). Success causes the target to feel as though the life is being drained form their bodies. In game terms, this gift subtracts one die from all Physical (and Appearance) rolls for the next scene. It also subtracts one from the difficulty of any Rage roll the target makes in that time. Vampires and other creatures of the like will reveal their undead nature while under the effects of this gift.<br /> <br /> Contagious Blight (Rank 1)<br /> Marred by their association with the dead, the necrotic, entropic essence of the Dark Umbra courses through the Dusk Walker\u2019s very essence, seeping out of their every pore like cold dark concentrated despair. This discharge of plasma from their flesh seeps into those they come in contact with, quickly causing violent nausea to grievous wounds.<br /> System: The Walker must concentrate for a turn, spend one Rage point, and then touch their target. The target immediately takes three levels of bashing or two levels of lethal damage. With the expenditure of a Willpower point in addition, one level of aggravated damage may be dealt instead. This damaged may be soaked and healed as normal. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:21:57-08:00","id":753958,"title":"","content":"I wrote a mini-tribebook for a new Tribe I intend to add to a future W20 game, I was riffing off the idea of W20 itself - that the apocalypse failed to manifest on time with the chronology of the old Apocalypse book and what the ramifications of that would be. The Snake Eaters tribe was the outcome, a tribe comprised of garou who came to the unwelcome conclusion that if they're going to have to keep up the fight for much longer at the current rate of attrition there might not be any left by the time the real Apocalyse does roll around, leaving Gaia unacceptably undefended. A lot was added based on suggestions from an rpg.net thread, like including the Perfect Metis as their leader to give a good reason why the other tribes wouldn't just tear them appart and the various camps are all based on suggestions for how their tribal philosophy might manifest. It's still a work in progress, haven't finished all the Gifts and Rites yet, but it's taking form.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'll leave a link to the google doc. here; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DDnVZzTr83LM7leO8SM2qOjAPwRGRKMzxeSA7pLhAvc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:46:24-08:00","id":753997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=753958#post753958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'll leave a link to the google doc. here; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DDnVZzTr83LM7leO8SM2qOjAPwRGRKMzxeSA7pLhAvc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I really like the concept of your new tribe. <br /> <br /> Autocannibalism looks like it was based off of the White Howler gift Blooding Fury from past Lives, I am a little curious why you choose to allow your version to be used more then once per scene?<br /> <br /> I also think that Born Angry should be a rank 3 gift. Most gifts that have to do with adding forms are done at this rank with other fera who have fewer forms. While your not giving them a new form, you are giving them greater control of their own forms. I love that it is a permanent effect, it really makes the players have to decide if they want to risk breaking the veil if they choose Crinos.<br /> <br /> Cool Blooded is a terrifying gift. The fact that they remember everything that happens during Thrall of the Wyrm and have full control of there capacities is dark. I am assuming them must still work on the impulses that Thrall normally imparts of those that succumb to it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:00:13-08:00","id":754033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=753997#post753997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, I really like the concept of your new tribe.<br /> <br /> Autocannibalism looks like it was based off of the White Howler gift Blooding Fury from past Lives, I am a little curious why you choose to allow your version to be used more then once per scene?<br /> <br /> I also think that Born Angry should be a rank 3 gift. Most gifts that have to do with adding forms are done at this rank with other fera who have fewer forms. While your not giving them a new form, you are giving them greater control of their own forms. I love that it is a permanent effect, it really makes the players have to decide if they want to risk breaking the veil if they choose Crinos.<br /> <br /> Cool Blooded is a terrifying gift. The fact that they remember everything that happens during Thrall of the Wyrm and have full control of there capacities is dark. I am assuming them must still work on the impulses that Thrall normally imparts of those that succumb to it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks, I wasn't familiar with Blooding Fury, so I'll consider adjusting Autocannibalism to match it approximately. Likewise I may end up changing Born Angry's level.<br /> <br /> As for Cold Blood I may change it to having no effect on the Thrall of the Wyrm... though it may be more interesting to basically cause them to act more like a NWoD Slasher temporarily - driven by dark impulses but still rational.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:17:35-08:00","id":754066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=753958#post753958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, I'll leave a link to the google doc. here; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1DDnVZzTr83LM7leO8SM2qOjAPwRGRKMzxeSA7pLhAvc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Really good write up and concept. The idea of seeking breeding rites, while accepting metis as buffers fits so well. And also, just the idea of a group of garou seeking another way to fight the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:06:43-08:00","id":754377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754066#post754066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really good write up and concept. The idea of seeking breeding rites, while accepting metis as buffers fits so well. And also, just the idea of a group of garou seeking another way to fight the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I missed this when i read through it the first time because i was just skimming... is this something new with W20? As far as I knew Pure Breed had nothing to do with breeding probabilities and kinfolk were tied to changing breed not tribe. So if you are a Kinfolk to the Fianna you still have the same possibility of breeding true with any other tribe, your offspring would just be lower in pure breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:33:18-08:00","id":754413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754377#post754377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I missed this when i read through it the first time because i was just skimming... is this something new with W20? As far as I knew Pure Breed had nothing to do with breeding probabilities and kinfolk were tied to changing breed not tribe. So if you are a Kinfolk to the Fianna you still have the same possibility of breeding true with any other tribe, your offspring would just be lower in pure breed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless it's changed, I was going by the rules in Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, where a kin's Pure Breed rating increases the likelihood of breeding true. I haven't seen anything to contradict this, but that book is admittedly a fair bit old right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T10:59:32-08:00","id":754537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754413#post754413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Unless it's changed, I was going by the rules in Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes, where a kin's Pure Breed rating increases the likelihood of breeding true. I haven't seen anything to contradict this, but that book is admittedly a fair bit old right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank You, I had never read that part. I will take a look at Unsung Hero's when i get home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:21:54-08:00","id":754581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754377#post754377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I missed this when i read through it the first time because i was just skimming... is this something new with W20? As far as I knew Pure Breed had nothing to do with breeding probabilities and kinfolk were tied to changing breed not tribe. So if you are a Kinfolk to the Fianna you still have the same possibility of breeding true with any other tribe, your offspring would just be lower in pure breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Random_Interrupt said, Kinfolk book gives (rather silly) rules how PB affects breeding. Silly, because purebreed makes it more likely for garou off-spring to happen the higher it is, while most of the setting assumes most garou don't have purebreed.<br /> <br /> But W20 also ties Purebreed to tribe. You have to be of the right tribe for your Purebreed to be counted, otherwise it is not. You still technically have it, but it has no mechanical effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:26:20-08:00","id":754591,"title":"","content":"It makes sense to me that purebreed would be tied to tribe. If a garou character leaves or never joins the tribe for which their purebreed reflect then they lose/never receive that bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:30:29-08:00","id":754599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754591#post754591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense to me that purebreed would be tied to tribe. If a garou character leaves or never joins the tribe for which their purebreed reflect then they lose/never receive that bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And it avoids the cases of Bone Gnawer having pb5 to Silver Fangs. Also, in an in-direct way, White Howler throwbacks don't mysteriously have pb5, since Lion or Whip-Poor-Will aren't supporting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:38:52-08:00","id":754608,"title":"","content":"Actually White Howler throwbacks are the only Black Spiral Dancers that can have Purebreed and it has to be Level 5, or am I not understanding what you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T11:51:56-08:00","id":754630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754608#post754608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually White Howler throwbacks are the only Black Spiral Dancers that can have Purebreed and it has to be Level 5, or am I not understanding what you mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but outside of BSDs, their breeding doesn't have mechanical effects at all. That is what I meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T19:33:18-08:00","id":755642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=754630#post754630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but outside of BSDs, their breeding doesn't have mechanical effects at all. That is what I meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't think that is true. Gaian Garou are effected by a BSD's Pure Breed and the same works the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T00:56:14-08:00","id":755968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=755642#post755642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually don't think that is true. Gaian Garou are effected by a BSD's Pure Breed and the same works the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm. That entirely depends. COnsidering that the BSD's can only have 0 or 5 Pure Breed that would mean that only the ones that look like White Howlers would get the bonus, and them looking that much like White Howlers would add problems that being more charismatic can not fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T01:22:51-08:00","id":756015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=755968#post755968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Erm. That entirely depends. COnsidering that the BSD's can only have 0 or 5 Pure Breed that would mean that only the ones that look like White Howlers would get the bonus, and them looking that much like White Howlers would add problems that being more charismatic can not fix.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about a garou with pure breed that has done the spiral tango? Does that wipe out the pure breed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:37:58-08:00","id":756253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=755642#post755642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually don't think that is true. Gaian Garou are effected by a BSD's Pure Breed and the same works the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually meant it as if the Howler Throwback -doesn't- join the dancers, but is a ronin/joins another tribe.<br /> <br /> As for purebred of other tribes who join the Dancers? I'd say they lose it post-haste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:48:45-08:00","id":756262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=756015#post756015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what about a garou with pure breed that has done the spiral tango? Does that wipe out the pure breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. If he keeps his mutations and interactions with the bad shit to a limit, I'd say he keeps his Pure Breed. It makes him a better infiltrator. Eventually, however, he will get gifts and mutations that will make it go bye bye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T05:19:47-08:00","id":756281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=756253#post756253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually meant it as if the Howler Throwback -doesn't- join the dancers, but is a ronin/joins another tribe.<br /> As for purebred of other tribes who join the Dancers? I'd say they lose it post-haste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I understand now and completely agree with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=756015#post756015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about a garou with pure breed that has done the spiral tango? Does that wipe out the pure breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree with Ana here, dancing the spiral is the same as renouncing your former tribe and being initiated into the Black Spiral Dancers. The moment you leave your previous tribe you lose your pure breed bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T06:09:49-08:00","id":756355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=756281#post756281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with Ana here, dancing the spiral is the same as renouncing your former tribe and being initiated into the Black Spiral Dancers. The moment you leave your previous tribe you lose your pure breed bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>One would think that the BSD's hiding among other Garou was not a thing then, since a purebreed would instantly look way less flashier and persuasive then he did before he danced the spiral. I can see it going down with the blessings, gifts and mutations of the Wyrm, but it's most likely a gradual process.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T08:43:32-08:00","id":756627,"title":"","content":"I think your absolutely right that when Garou with Pure Breed fall it is harder for them to hide what has happened. I don't think that such an event should be moderated. That said, maybe Whippoorwill could grant these special bastards a unique gift or fetish that allows them to maintain the illusion of their pure breed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T10:39:26-08:00","id":756880,"title":"","content":"Then again, maybe purebreed mimicry isn't a good thing. After all, a BSD who wants to convince someone to fall has to be subtle. Purebreed will always put you on the spot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:03:52-08:00","id":756941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=756015#post756015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But what about a garou with pure breed that has done the spiral tango? Does that wipe out the pure breed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Word in W20 is that Pure Breed is a mysticla trait inherited from generations after generations supporting the same Tribe. W20 core mentions that if you renounce your Tribe, either by taking your Rite of Passage with a different Tribe than the one you get your blood from or later in life by way of the Rite of Renunciation, your PB goes bye bye. So it's no0t that dancign the Black Spiral makes you lose it; anyway you shift your allegiance makes you lose it.<br /> <br /> W20 core, page 138. Actually the book misses a reference for what happens when you renunciate your Tribe as an adult (it also misses a Rite for that - as written the Rite of Renunciation works only for Auspice) but it's safe to assume that if your totem can strip Pure Breed from you even before you join its Tribe then it can do the same for a turncoat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T13:18:55-08:00","id":759246,"title":"","content":"Just putting a few new Gifts for my Snake Eaters tribebook project up for critique as the last round proved really helpful.<br /> <br /> First off is a relatively low-level Gift, which was to take the place of Born Angry, which I upped to level 3 on Derzhuzad's advisal;<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sonar (Level Two) -</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> The user of this Gift clicks their tongue or whistles and uses the rebounding sound waves to build up an image of all solid objects around them. By spending 1 Gnosis they are able to see all solid objects and materialised spirits within 10 meters per success on a \u2018Perception + Alertness\u2019 roll, even around corners and behind objects. Enclosed structures normally block their contents from the garou\u2019s sight unless they make physical contact with one of its surfaces and knock or tap it, allowing \u201csight\u201d into the other side up to 5 meters per success. A whale, bat or dolphin spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <br /> Then we're on to a couple of level fours, I'm pretty happy with Abominate but I don't know if Change Minds is kosher;</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Change Mind (Level Four) -</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">With this potent hypnotic Gift the Snake Eater can change a person\u2019s beliefs and opinions on a subject by staring into their eyes and telling them what they believe. A Cobra spirit teaches this gift.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">System:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Spend a point of Gnosis and roll \u2018Manipulation + Empathy\u2019 vs the victim\u2019s Willpower. The storyteller assigns a difficulty to the roll based on the scale of the change made. This can be as low as 4 to finally settle the Coke vs. Pepsi debate or as high as 9 to change the underpinnings of someone\u2019s personality like a devout religious belief or vociferously-held political stance. The victim may spend Willpower points to cancel out the Snake Eater\u2019s successes but if the Snake Eater wins the opposed roll the newly revised opinion immediately takes root in their mind. The revised opinion can still change over time in response to challenge and evidence like any other but can be hard to budge, especially in a stubborn person - mechanically, the victim will spend Willpower points to defend the revised opinion as if it were their own. Making a person believe something demonstrably false, like the sky is orange or water flows uphill, requires a roll at difficulty 10 and doesn\u2019t tend to last long, but the results are hilarious.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Abominate (Level Four) -</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">One of the Snake Eater\u2019s most disturbing Gifts allows them to expose themselves directly to the pain of Gaia for but a moment, the spiritual agony reverberating through their bodies and triggering an involuntary shapeshift. The resultant shifted form is invariably somehow </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">wrong</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">... but still empowered by Gaia\u2019s own spirit. In addition to its obvious uses, a Snake Eater under the effects of this Gift can easily pass for a Black Spiral Dancer in their crinos form or a fomori in their homid or glabro, for better or worse. A pain-spirit teaches this Gift.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">System:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Spend a point of Rage and make a \u2018Stamina + Primal Urge\u2019 roll, using one success per form shifted through as normal for shapechanging. For each excess success the Snake Eater adds one of the following bonuses, in the form of some monstrous physical mutation. Unless otherwise specified the same mutation cannot be selected twice;</span></span></span><ul><li>Increase the damage of claw or bite attacks by +1 or gain the ability to make bite or claw attacks in a form that does not normally have one (massive snaggleteeth and knife-sized claws)</li> <li>Increase soak by +2 (thick, leathery hide, scales or bony plates)</li> <li>Add a point to any one physical Attribute (grotesquely bulging muscles, disturbing multi-jointedness)</li> <li>Decrease the difficulty of Climbing or Swimming rolls by -2 (spider-like claws, webbed hands and feet)</li> <li>Decrease the difficulty of rolls related to one sense by -2 (batlike ears, bloodshot multi-pupiled eyes)</li> <li>Grow extra limbs, as the fomori power (extra arms or tentacles, long prehensile tail)</li> </ul>Finally the biggies, the level fives;<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Turn Back The Wheel (Level Five) -</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> The Snake Eaters\u2019 totem Ouroboros is a spirit of, amongst other things, time, renewal and hope. In moments that seem the most hopeless, a werewolf with this Gift can snatch victory from the jaws of defeat by reversing time a scant few seconds, allowing them to do over their actions now forewarned. An avatar of Ouroboros teaches this Gift.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">System:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Spend a point of Gnosis after your turn is complete, you may rewind time to the beginning of the turn with all effects that occurred since the start undone. You may then take your turn over again and may choose to take different actions. At a cost of two Gnosis points you may confer this benefit to another player. This Gift may not be used more than once per round.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Perfection (Level Five) -</span></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> The Perfect Metis himself granted this Gift to the Snake Eaters, with it the user can briefly bring their entire being into perfect triatic alignment, becoming a being of spiritual and physical purity as life was intended to be without the diminishment of the Wyld, the madness of the Weaver or the corruption of the Wyrm. The Garou assumes an idealised version of their crinos form, their fur markings razor-sharp and brightly coloured, their countenance wise and noble rather than terrifying, moving with impossible grace as if the world posed them no obstacle. No spirit teaches this Gift, it can only be learned from another Snake Eater who has it.</span></span></span> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:12px\">System:</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Spend 1 each of Gnosis, Rage and Willpower, this is an exception to the normal rules regarding spending Rage and Gnosis in the same turn. You immediately shift to crinos and for the rest of the scene, or until you leave crinos form, all your actions gain 1 automatic success.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:58:20-08:00","id":759584,"title":"","content":"Any reason you didn't use the existing gift mechanics for these gifts? It seems like they accomplish what you are trying to do.<br /> Sonar - Ears of the Bat (Black Spiral Dancer Rank 2)<br /> Turn Back the Wheel - Sidestep Death (Silverfang Rank 4)<br /> <br /> Abominate seems powerful for a 4 but I can't think of anything off the top of my head right now thats comparable, I think 1 mutation per success is a lot though.<br /> <br /> Perfection seems fine to me, its powerful but it limited to scene so I don't see anything wrong with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T00:39:39-08:00","id":759805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=759584#post759584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any reason you didn't use the existing gift mechanics for these gifts? It seems like they accomplish what you are trying to do.<br /> Sonar - Ears of the Bat (Black Spiral Dancer Rank 2)<br /> Turn Back the Wheel - Sidestep Death (Silverfang Rank 4)</div> </div> </div> </div>Just wasn't aware of them, there's a LOT of Gifts out there.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks for the heads up on those. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=759584#post759584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abominate seems powerful for a 4 but I can't think of anything off the top of my head right now thats comparable, I think 1 mutation per success is a lot though.<br /> <br /> Perfection seems fine to me, its powerful but it limited to scene so I don't see anything wrong with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, here's a list of the modifications I think I'm going to make;<br /> <br /> Replace Sonar with Ears of the Bat, that seems an obvious one.<br /> Increase Abominate to a Level 5<br /> Remove Turn Back The Wheel and replace it with Sidestep Death in the former level 4 slot held by Abominate<br /> <br /> Also on reflection, I think Perfection should have a secondary effect of temporarily suppressing metis deformities and battle scar penalties. It's not a massive bonus but it's thematically suitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T04:21:34-08:00","id":761361,"title":"","content":"Yeah there are a lot of gifts, I am currently playing with the Domini Canis concept from earlier in the thread, so I had been digging through gifts trying to get a rough gift lists together. <br /> <br /> I like the changes, balancing wise I don't see any issue in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:10:23-08:00","id":761413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=761361#post761361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah there are a lot of gifts, I am currently playing with the Domini Canis concept from earlier in the thread, so I had been digging through gifts trying to get a rough gift lists together.<br /> <br /> I like the changes, balancing wise I don't see any issue in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool, would like to see them when they're done. Between the Domini Canis and the Lycaon also mentioned earlier I can't help but think a fanbook presenting a whole new alt.universe Garou Nation would be a cool thing to have.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: Also, found this bitchin' pic that made me think &quot;Well, this is obviously a Dark Ages Domini Canis in crinos&quot;;<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://pre13.deviantart.net/4a1d/th/pre/i/2013/221/6/e/the_werewolf_s_redemption_by_liuhao726-d6hcnv0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8485,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","user":"Random_Interrupt","date":". 11-09-2015, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T06:15:43-08:00","id":761420,"title":"","content":"I am not sure how much I like my back story for the Domini Canis right now. I like the premise I came up but i feel I am missing something in the history. The link below is a very rough draft.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8GVz-RVG_GBUVFmbTNFZkFuc2M/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8GVz-RVG_GBUVFmbTNFZkFuc2M/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8GVz-RVG_GBUVFmbTNFZkFuc2M/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8GVz-RVG_GBUVFmbTNFZkFuc2M/view?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-09T13:23:19-08:00","id":761675,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see some more on these sub-tribes. Maybe the Singing Dogs could have howl/singing based gifts like siren songs and howls that can shatter glass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T04:32:07-08:00","id":762193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=761675#post761675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see some more on these sub-tribes. Maybe the Singing Dogs could have howl/singing based gifts like siren songs and howls that can shatter glass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which sub-tribes? you said 'these' implying more then one. As for the singing dogs I think there lack of membership is why we see so few gifts from them. Elders in the tribe act almost as a record of what spirits teach what gifts. With only 4 members I have to assume that a lot of tribal knowledge has been lost to them for a long time. If I was working a full gifts list I would probably pull form the White Howler, Red Talon, and Gilliard gifts lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T05:54:03-08:00","id":762230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=761420#post761420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure how much I like my back story for the Domini Canis right now. I like the premise I came up but i feel I am missing something in the history. The link below is a very rough draft.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8GVz-RVG_GBUVFmbTNFZkFuc2M/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B8G...ew?usp=sharing</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just realized that for some reason my rough draft of their gifts didn't sync so I will work on the later. I spent a little time reworking the tribal definition, It not finished yet and I am still not sure how much how much ancient history I want to give them.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Added gifts from the unsynced version to the posted version. They are no where near final, I already plan to make a change to the rank 2 gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","user":"Derzhuzad","date":". 11-11-2015, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T11:48:56-08:00","id":764251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=353934#post353934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got two, one an older tribe idea, a sort of Lancea Sanctum for Garou. And another a historical take on Glass Walkers.<br /> <b><i>Domini Canis</i></b><br /> <i>&quot;Let the way of God guide you in your battles&quot;<br /> <br /> Most of the garou nation is quite pagan. They know what job gaia fullfills in their lives, they know her rules and her laws.<br /> <br /> The hounds, however, doubt the truth of this. They believe God created all, Gaia,Triat, and something went wrong. Very wrong. And it is the garou nation's sacret duty to fix things. The hounds are one of the more confusing pariah tribes, united by religion and often being one of the most profilic tribes in supporting human rights. But when the battle calls, hounds have been seen in the front lines just as well. The tribe fully believes in their own dogma, and thus, they see their mission as absolute, no few times has a Shadow Lord or a Red Talon felt the claws of the Hounds.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately to anyone thinking to use the hounds using their religion, the hounds do not see themselves as 'human' anymore than other tribes. In fact, they denounce that notion quite violently, and any garou daring to pray the human way will be considered a blasbemer.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ok Ana, I have rewritten the history of this Tribe 3 or 4 times now, I think lol, I have lost count. I think the document holds true to your original idea but your input would be great, the gift list isn't final. There are a few changes I want to make but I wanted a good base to start from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:13:52-08:00","id":764276,"title":"","content":"I really dig it, especially the whole Patriarch betrayal added in.<br /> <br /> I really REALLY don't want to say anything about gifts, simply because I'm bad at mechanics XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:18:28-08:00","id":764282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764276#post764276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dig it, especially the whole Patriarch betrayal added in.<br /> <br /> I really REALLY don't want to say anything about gifts, simply because I'm bad at mechanics XD</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I will add the patriarch betrayal back then, I thought it may have deviated to much from the original concept so I rewrote the whole thing earlier. Shouldn't be to hard though, the newest write up is just less about ancient history more a general overview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:36:16-08:00","id":764294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764282#post764282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I will add the patriarch betrayal back then, I thought it may have deviated to much from the original concept so I rewrote the whole thing earlier. Shouldn't be to hard though, the newest write up is just less about ancient history more a general overview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is a factor in the setting.<br /> <br /> Honestly, you've done good work with it, no need to ask for my opinion 'bout it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:41:24-08:00","id":764301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764294#post764294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is a factor in the setting.<br /> Honestly, you've done good work with it, no need to ask for my opinion 'bout it.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did you think of totem? <br /> <br /> Your concept, I don't want to deviate to far from it.<br /> <br /> I have added back their older history and I have also given them a Glyph. <br /> <br /> Hope you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:43:15-08:00","id":764306,"title":"","content":"I dunno if I've posted these yet, but here are some Uratha tribes translated to Apocalypse setting, if the two worlds merged;<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons.</b><br /> Unlike the Nation, Tribes of the Moon were never exactly geared for war in a global sense. So it is no wonder that their tribe of War is less extreme. The Blood Talons stand amongs the tribes of War as the soldiers of the Nation, seeking Glory in much simpler and down-to-Earth ways than their fellow tribes. Let the Get have their glorious Valhalla, Furies their causes and the Fianna their passion. Blood Talons care only for the fitness of a warrior. Not unlike the Fenrir, however, is their way of constantly testing one another. But their motives are entirely different. The Blood Talons want the job -done-, and as such it isn't at all unsual for the tribe of Bear to sacrifice themselves for even a Phyrric victory.<br /> <br /> The tribe in general has trouble accepting defeat,owing to their old tribal oath; &quot;Offer no surrender that you would not accept&quot;. And with a great foe like the Wyrm against them, the Blood Talons find little reason to surrender.<br /> Totem: Bear. Bear is a patient totem, saddened by his loss of children, but glad his guardianship is again requested.<br /> Appearance: As career warriors, the Blood Talons favour simplicity in everything. As with all tribes of the moon, the tribe lacks pure breed entirely, and as such cubs from other tribes often show their breeding quiter clearly. Blood Talons are wiry and strong in lupus, with scars or scarified glyphs on their body. The tribe has taken a special kind of interest in the Rite of Wounding.<br /> Willpower: 4<br /> Starting Gifts: Camouflage, Razor Claws, and Resist Pain.<br /> <br /> Quote: &quot;Yeah yeah, keep babblin' 'bout your ancestors. I'll the there, my blade in the gut of the foe&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows.</b><br /> The mystics of the Tribes of the Moon, the Bone Shadows would have fit in the best among the Tribes to the Nation. Unfortunately, with the lack of ancient lines and pacts with spirits, and their assosication with death willingly, the Shadows often teeter between Pariah and Mystic tribes. Bone Shadows, much like the Uktena, dig deep into the Umbra to find answers. However, they do it for the sake of Wisdom alone. With little reason to care about breeding and lines, and with pacts to spirits all ready in place, the Shadows are giddily digging up secrets they once were unable to access.<br /> <br /> Of course, their digging has caused troubles with other tribes. That and their former oath; &quot;Pay each spirit in kind.&quot; The Shadows have little reason to treat an uncoperative spirit well, no matter what brood it belongs to.<br /> Totem: Crow. Once a proud member of Grandfather Thunder's brood, Crow found the Bone Shadows a great tribe to watch over.<br /> Appearance: Bone Shadows in their wolf form are thin things, often adorned with all kind of trinkets from whoknows where. Their furs tend to be pale from the constant assiocation with death.<br /> Willpower: 3<br /> Starting Gifts: Sense Wyrm, Sense Magic, and Silence.<br /> <br /> Quote: &quot;Little Bane, you are a spirit as any other, and you have been disturbing my pack. Time to pay&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters.</b><br /> <br /> Most of the Nation tribes see the Glass Walkers as an abomination, garou who give themselves willingly for Weaver to corrupt. So when the Iron Masters came around, the Nation expected the strange new tribe to be an exact copy of the Walkers. However, where the Walkers live in cities because they have always guarded humanity, the Iron Masters only seek to do things in new ways. The tribe is in some ways better and far worse than Walkers could ever be, Iron Masters are not only interested in the cities, yet they respect no tradition other than guarding their territory. An Iron Master will experiment how far they can go modifying rites, how bizarre fetishes can they make and there are even rumors of groups of Iron Masters who seek to understand what truly makes the metis metis.<br /> Yet, the tribe is known to be insanely territorial, a fact that makes their otherwise lax morals seem bizarre. The poor souls that arrive to Iron Master ground unnannounced tend to end up beaten to a bloody pulp.<br /> Totem: Fox, the clever red coated hunter gives the Iron Masters their cunning and guile.<br /> Appearance: Iron Masters are a varied group, they are rural shamans, businessmen or honor bound warriors. Yet all work to break the status quo. Iron Masters in the wolf forms are often highly stylized, yet they lack the Walker doggishness almost entirely. Tattoos that show on fur are common.<br /> Willpower: 4<br /> Starting Gifts:<br /> Quote: &quot;Do you like it? It's a eagle and rat spirit whip. What, why's that wrong?&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:45:06-08:00","id":764308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764306#post764306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno if I've posted these yet, but here are some Uratha tribes translated to Apocalypse setting, if the two worlds merged;</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you not like the translation from the Translation guide?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:45:26-08:00","id":764310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764301#post764301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you think of totem?<br /> <br /> Your concept, I don't want to deviate to far from it.<br /> <br /> I have added back their older history and I have also given them a Glyph.<br /> <br /> Hope you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the glyph is neat ^^<br /> <br /> The totem is interesting, where'd you dug it up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764308#post764308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did you not like the translation from the Translation guide?</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did, I literally took the totems and beginning gifts from there. I just wrote them as if they used to -be- the uratha tribes before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T12:50:00-08:00","id":764316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764310#post764310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, the glyph is neat ^^<br /> <br /> The totem is interesting, where'd you dug it up?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I made it, kind of. More like I translated it from history into the game. Aion/Chronos/Father Time/Death are all considered one of the ancient Gods, often confused with the Titan Kronos. This was before I read shattered dreams, so I am glad they went with Kronos otherwise I was completely out of ideas for this tribe. Eternity seemed like the only thing bigger then Gaia <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T02:57:26-08:00","id":764804,"title":"","content":"Their tribal glyph translates to something along the lines of &quot;Fire Friends&quot; or &quot;Fiery Allies&quot;, so I wonder if they should have some Gifts related to fire? Sort of witch-burning redemptionist type stuff. Master of Fire and Kiss of Helios are obvious ones, but maybe also some variation of the White Howler's &quot;White Fire&quot; Gift as a level 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T04:30:10-08:00","id":764844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764804#post764804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their tribal glyph translates to something along the lines of &quot;Fire Friends&quot; or &quot;Fiery Allies&quot;, so I wonder if they should have some Gifts related to fire? Sort of witch-burning redemptionist type stuff. Master of Fire and Kiss of Helios are obvious ones, but maybe also some variation of the White Howler's &quot;White Fire&quot; Gift as a level 5?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Domini Canis is a real order in the church. St. Dominic's mother had a vision of a dog carrying a fiery torch to set fire upon the world before his birth. I drew from that for their glyph, as their purpose is to spread across Gaia and purify the taint.<br /> <br /> I do need to update the gifts though because the original list in the write up is not my working set. I will be pulling a few gifts from the Grondr that are more 'purifier' like gifts.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I have made some changes to the gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","user":"Derzhuzad","date":". 11-13-2015, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:08:54-08:00","id":764859,"title":"","content":"Cool, some kind of flaming torch would make a neat tribal fetish. Maybe with an effect like burning away wyrm corruption with its light, banishing banes or rousing Rage in allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:50:35-08:00","id":764882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=764859#post764859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool, some kind of flaming torch would make a neat tribal fetish. Maybe with an effect like burning away wyrm corruption with its light, banishing banes or rousing Rage in allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hadn't thought of fetish/talon items yet lol. The other tribe I have been working on is just a Gifts and Rites list even though I have them all worked out in my head. This is probably the most fleshed out product i have had in a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T12:35:20-08:00","id":768664,"title":"","content":"Added a new section for Camps and 2 new totems (Bull and Bat). Seeing as they didn't bring the Children of Bat into W20 I figured this was the perfect tribe to make peace with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T15:26:15-07:00","id":942272,"title":"","content":"Years ago (about 10 of them) I played with the idea of a tribe that took a sort of Judeo-Christian view to Garou spirituality. Kind of like the Garou answer to paladins and inquisitors who are guided by a fierce love for Gaia that makes them heartfelt yet vicious enough to tear off a Vampire's head in the name of the &quot;glorious burden&quot; they've accepted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T22:51:58-07:00","id":944144,"title":"","content":"I posted this in a different thread already but here it is.<br /> <br /> one of my house retcons I have waiting for the new edition is that after the perfect metis was born, the metis that were born during and after the 90s weren't sterile, and a group of them have formed their own tribe that only accepts members that are either metis or born to metis parents. They're developing a stable of kinfolk among the neurodiversity and disability communities and earned the grudging respect of the other tribes when they dealt a major blow to the wyrm when they managed to get evidence that O'Tolley's was using fake &quot;clean&quot; slaughterhouses to trick the public while the real ones were places of horror into the hands of none other than Temple motherfucking Grandin right before she was set to be part of a Nightly show panel. The result was not only that O'tolleys got smacked with a bunch of lawsuits, but also that Pentax has become a household name known for shady business (thanks to the shows of the various daily show alumni focusing so much on them), though most people still don't know about the spiritual corruption.<br /> <br /> Said as yet unnamed tribe is part of the Concordat of Stars, partly because they understand the potential of human tech to mitigate disability and partly because is no fucking way a tribe of disability rights focused metis would ever be part of the same faction as the Fianna.<br /> <br /> I want their gifts to based around taking away and nullifying things their enemies rely on, particularly support networks (disabled people certainly understand the value of a support network).<br /> <br /> Their strategies for fighting the wyrm are odd, but would make perfect sense to other garou if the tribe could only figure out how to explain them to the other. However, once the rest of the garou see the results, it all becomes clear.<br /> <br /> Their totem is the spirit of the first metis herself, who was eventually killed by first teams sent after her after she stole a large amount of wyrm tainted sugar from Pentax subsidiary Fruitas LTD (Pentax's answer to United Fruit), and then used said sugar to gum up pipelines at various Endron facilities. After her death, she ascended to become the totem of the tribe and that is what I have so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T15:03:08-07:00","id":990653,"title":"","content":"I think it might be worth mentioning that Shattered Dreams touches a little bit on early tribes. Not -much-, but it does mention names of early proto-tribes that may have split into the modern ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7621-threadwrought","name":"Threadwrought","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T06:03:21-07:00","id":990926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Threadwrought</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=990653#post990653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it might be worth mentioning that Shattered Dreams touches a little bit on early tribes. Not -much-, but it does mention names of early proto-tribes that may have split into the modern ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually used that information when developing one of my subtribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}